    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\nI implemented the daily-limit rule following the existing capacity/uniqueness pattern, keeping structural impact minimal \u2014 three brand-new small classes (each a single method with no surrounding class complexity) plus one new escalation YAML, and I only edited **one** existing file:\n\n- `RequireDailyCapacity` \u2014 counts owners whose `registrationDate` is today; throws `DailyLimitException` at 100+.\n- `DailyLimitException` (checked) + `DailyLimitExceptionHandler` \u2014 responds **429 Too Many Requests**.\n- `...DailyLimitException.yml` \u2014 registers the handler.\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 a new `dailyLimit` step wired after `capacity`, before `build` (so the cap is enforced before an owner is constructed/saved).\n\nI did not touch any existing function class, so no high-WMC method was modified. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
